.TH QVREC 1 "$Date: 2000/08/28 19:41:28 $" "Local" "Local commands"
.UC 4
.SH NAME
qvrec \- upload pictures to a Casio QV-10 digital camera.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.ad l
.B qvrec
[
.BI \-D \ ttydevice
]
[
.BI \-S \ speed
]
[
.B \-hv
]
file1.cam file2.cam ...
.ad b
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page applies to
.B qvrec
version 0.95 by ken-ichi HAYASHI and Jun-ichiro "itojun" ITOH.
.PP
.B qvrec
allows the computer to upload CAM format pictures to the Casio QV-10 digital
camera.
Use entirely at your own risk.
The CAM format is proprietary to Casio.
.P
The camera can take up to 96 pictures, each at 320x240 24-bit
pixels. It can be linked to the serial port of a computer using the
supplied cable (see
.BR qvplay (1)
for wiring changes needed for some machines).
.PP
If the camera does not respond, switch it off and then on again to do
a 'hard' reset.  
If the transfer times out, try using a slower speed.
.PP
All pictures should be 480x240 pixels.
.SH OPTIONS
Options are processed from left to right so it is important to set the
serial line and speed first.
.IP "\fB\-D\fP \fIttydevice\fP"
Specify the serial port to use. Something like \fI/dev/ttyS0\fP on 
.B Unix
and \fICOM1\fP on less sophisticated systems.
The default is \fI/dev/qvtty\fP.
.IP "\fB\-S\fP \fIspeed\fP"
Specify the baud rate for the transfer. Possible values are
{normal, mid, high, top, light} or {1,2,3,4,5} for a corresponding
{9600, 19200, 38400, 57600, 115200} baud rate.
\'light speed' is supported in Linux, OS2, and Win NT/95.
With Old Linux, use 
.B setserial(1)
to achieve lightspeed e.g.
.RS
.PP
.nf
  setserial /dev/cua1 spd_hi	# set 57600baud
  qvrec -S top file1.cam
or
  setserial /dev/cua1 spd_vhi	# set 115200baud
  qvrec -S light file2.cam
.fi
.PP
If you are using a PC/AT compatible computer, you will need a 16550A compatible
serial controller to use more than 19200 baud (the 'mid' setting).
.RE
.IP "\fB\-h\fP"
Print a help message and exit.
Report camera revision (?)
.IP "\fB\-v\fP"
Verbosely reports upload information on 
.B stderr. 
Reported information is uploaded bytes, not a filesize.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.SH FILES
.SH BUGS
Fine mode picture of QV-100/200/300 and QV-700/770 is not supported.
